1.Build Production Artifacts Locally:Build the optimized production bundles locally on your development machine:Bash# 1. Frontend: create production bundle (generates ./dist)
npm run build

# 2. Backend: build executable JAR (generates build/libs/*.jar)
./gradlew clean build -x test
Verification: Check that the frontend generated a dist/ directory with index.html and the backend created an executable file in build/libs/app.jar (exclude plain -plain.jar archives).2.Transfer Artifacts to Debian 12:Log into your server, create a project directory, and use rsync or scp from your local machine to transfer the files:Bash# On Debian server:
mkdir -p ~/app/frontend-dist ~/app/backend

# From your local terminal:
scp build/libs/*.jar user@your_server_ip:~/app/backend/app.jar
scp -r dist/* user@your_server_ip:~/app/frontend-dist/
Verification: Run ls -la ~/app/backend and ls -la ~/app/frontend-dist on the server to ensure app.jar and index.html are present.3.Install Docker on Debian 12:Install Docker and the Docker Compose plugin using Debian's official repository tools:Bashsudo apt update
sudo apt install -y ca-certificates curl gnupg
sudo install -m 0755 -d /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/debian/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
sudo chmod a+r /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg

echo \
  "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/debian \
  $(. /etc/os-release && echo "$VERSION_CODENAME") stable" | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-compose-plugin
Verification: Run docker compose version and verify it prints the installed version.4.Configure Docker and Nginx on the Server:Inside ~/app, create the configuration files for your containers:~/app/backend/DockerfileDockerfileFROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY app.jar app.jar
EXPOSE 8080
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
(Adjust 21 to your project's Java version: 17, 21, etc.)~/app/nginx.confNginxserver {
    listen 80;
    server_name localhost;

    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html index.htm;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://backend:8080/;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}
~/app/docker-compose.ymlYAMLservices:
  backend:
    build: ./backend
    container_name: app_backend
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      - SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=prod
    expose:
      - "8080"

  frontend:
    image: nginx:alpine
    container_name: app_frontend
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "80:80"
    volumes:
      - ./frontend-dist:/usr/share/nginx/html:ro
      - ./nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:ro
    depends_on:
      - backend
Verification: Ensure docker-compose.yml, nginx.conf, backend/Dockerfile, and both asset folders sit in ~/app.5.Start Services and Validate:Build the backend image and run the entire stack in detached mode:Bashcd ~/app
sudo docker compose up -d --build
Verification: Run sudo docker compose ps to verify both containers report status Up. Open http://your_server_ip in a browser to confirm the UI loads and API calls route cleanly to your backend.


